 "notes": "Cross-sectional set transformer on the 10 champion features: each date's whole universe (~1,500 stocks) is one attention set, so a stock's score is conditioned on the full cross-section (the mechanism behind the cs_rank_* features, learned). BCE on label_beat_mkt_20d, one date per optimiser step, AdamW 5e-4, max 30 epochs, patience 5 on inner-val AUC (last 15% of train dates, purged 20 sessions). HALVING RULE APPLIED: the first full-spec epoch took 67 s on the smallest fold (136 dates) with box load ~8.5 on 4 cores, projecting >90 s/epoch for the larger folds, so d_model 64->32 and each training step uses a random 50% of the date's stocks (val/test use the full set). INTERPRETATION: Fails: CV 0.5197 +/- 0.035 with April and May below 0.50 (0.493/0.493) and a big July (0.578) -- the regime-bet profile of the sequence models, not stable selection. The label is already cross-sectional (beat the median) and the cs_rank_* features already normalise across stocks, so attention over ~1,450 names has little left to add, while 140-210 training dates (one optimiser step each) give it far more capacity than data; early stopping on the break-straddling tail (fold 2026-06 inner-val AUC <= 0.44) is the same trap. Run at the halved setting (d_model 32, 50% of each date's stocks per training step). Holdout 0.501, rank-IC NW t 0.70 (not significant); its score is a low-vol / near-52w-high factor (atr_pct -0.59, dist_52w_high +0.56).",
